This repository contains Foldnite proprietary intellectual property, technical
research records, valuation materials, invention disclosures, prior-art records,
architecture documentation, claim-oriented materials, internal governance
materials and related corporate documentation (collectively, the "Proprietary
Materials").

This license is an internal, restricted-use license. It is NOT an open-source
license and does NOT grant the public a right to copy, modify, fork, distribute,
publish, sublicense, sell, host, mirror, repackage, commercially exploit, or
otherwise use the Proprietary Materials except as expressly authorized in
writing by Foldnite.

1. AUTHORIZED USERS

Authorized Users are limited to:

- active Foldnite employees or officers acting within assigned duties ("Authorized
  Employees"); and
- non-employee individuals expressly approved in writing by an authorized Foldnite
  representative, and covered by a signed written agreement that incorporates
  this restricted-use regime and defines the permitted purpose, repositories,
  data scope, duration, security duties, confidentiality, IP treatment, and
  return/deletion obligations ("Approved Affiliate Users").

An Approved Affiliate User receives no general permission merely from this
LICENSE. The separate signed agreement must explicitly authorize the relevant
access and use. Access must be least-privilege, project-scoped, and removed when
the authorization expires or the work ends.

A person is NOT an Authorized User merely because they:

- can view, clone, fork, cache, mirror, index, or otherwise retrieve the
  repository through GitHub or another service;
- appear on a team roster or hold an organization/repository membership;
- are described as a contractor, consultant, advisor, customer, supplier,
  partner, investor, community member, contributor, researcher, or affiliate; or
- have signed an NDA without the separate access/use and IP terms required for
  the relevant work.

2. LIMITED INTERNAL LICENSE

Subject to this license and any applicable Foldnite employment, confidentiality,
invention-assignment, security, information-governance, and internal-use
agreements, an Authorized User may, only within their documented authorization and solely
for legitimate Foldnite internal business, research, legal, IP, engineering,
valuation, security, or development purposes:

- access and read the Proprietary Materials;
- reproduce the Proprietary Materials as reasonably necessary for internal work;
- modify and maintain Proprietary Materials for internal Foldnite purposes;
- create internal derivative works, analyses, claim charts, evidence bundles,
  valuation models, and technical records; and
- maintain internal copies required for development, audit, legal review,
  security, backup, compliance, or corporate governance.

3. PROHIBITED ACTIONS

Except with an applicable signed written authorization from Foldnite, no person may
perform the following actions. An Authorized User may do only the minimal acts
expressly required by the permitted scope; an Authorized Employee must act within
assigned duties, and an Approved Affiliate User must act strictly within the
external authorization:

- copy, reproduce, republish, or redistribute the Proprietary Materials;
- publish substantial portions of the Proprietary Materials outside Foldnite;
- fork, mirror, rehost, or create an external derivative repository;
- sell, lease, rent, sublicense, assign, transfer, or commercially exploit the
  Proprietary Materials;
- provide the Proprietary Materials or access to them to a third party;
- use the Proprietary Materials to build a competing product, service,
  architecture, scientific workflow, evidence system, valuation system, or
  intellectual-property management system;
- disclose confidential or non-public technical, business, scientific, legal,
  valuation, security, customer, contributor, or operational information
  contained in or derived from the Proprietary Materials;
- use Foldnite proprietary invention disclosures, claim concepts, architecture,
  schemas, workflows, mission logic, validation logic, valuation methodology,
  evidence structures, or deployment patterns to create a substantially
  equivalent external product or service;
- remove or alter copyright, licensing, attribution, security, confidentiality,
  provenance, or proprietary notices; or
- file, prosecute, license, assign, or otherwise assert intellectual-property
  rights based on Foldnite Proprietary Materials without express written
  authorization from Foldnite.

4. SPECIAL RULE FOR INVENTION DISCLOSURES AND PRIOR ART MATERIALS

Technical disclosures, invention records, claim-oriented documents,
architecture descriptions, evidence bundles, prior-art records, valuation
materials, and patent-oriented claim matrices are proprietary corporate records.
Their presence in a public Git repository does not constitute a public license
to reproduce, commercialize, adapt, or exploit the underlying Foldnite concepts.

Nothing in this section states that publication of a document creates a patent,
patent application, copyright registration, trade secret, or other exclusive
right. Patentability, inventorship, priority, novelty, enablement, ownership,
assignment, and enforceability are determined under applicable law and the
relevant legal instruments.

5. THIRD-PARTY AND OPEN-SOURCE MATERIALS

This license applies only to Proprietary Materials that Foldnite owns or is
legally entitled to license under these terms.

Third-party libraries, frameworks, SDKs, fonts, assets, datasets, scientific
software, model weights, documentation, trademarks, public specifications,
open-source components, upstream repositories, and other third-party materials
