6. MIXED-LICENSE REPOSITORY RULE

Where this repository contains materials under different rights regimes, the
following hierarchy applies:

- Foldnite-owned Proprietary Materials: this license;
- third-party/open-source materials: their applicable upstream license;
- separately licensed customer, partner, contributor, or research materials:
  their applicable written agreement or license;
- trademarks, likenesses, characters, brands, and other third-party IP: the
  applicable rights-holder terms.

Repository access does not convert third-party material into Foldnite property
and does not convert Foldnite property into third-party material.

7. NO OPEN-SOURCE GRANT FOR PROPRIETARY MATERIALS

The Proprietary Materials are not released under MIT, Apache, BSD, GPL, AGPL,
LGPL, Creative Commons, or any other open-source or public license merely
because this repository is publicly accessible.

Any file intentionally released by Foldnite under a separate open-source or
public license remains subject to that license and must be identified as such.

A later internal policy or license does not retroactively revoke rights already
granted under a valid earlier open-source license.

8. CONTRIBUTIONS AND AUTHORSHIP

Contributions to this repository do not automatically grant a contributor or
third party ownership of Foldnite Proprietary Materials.

Ownership, inventorship, assignment, confidentiality, moral-rights treatment,
and contribution rights are governed by the contributor's applicable employment
agreement, invention-assignment agreement, contributor agreement, contractor
agreement, license, or separate written instrument with Foldnite.

Where authorship or inventorship is material to an IP claim, Foldnite may retain
restricted legal records mapping technical identities, commit history, reviews,
assignments, signatures, and corporate roles.

9. EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION

An Authorized Employee's permission automatically terminates when the person's
employment with Foldnite ends, unless a separate written authorization is provided.
An Approved Affiliate User's permission ends when the applicable written
authorization or governing agreement expires or terminates.

Upon termination, the former employee must stop using the Proprietary Materials
and return or securely destroy Foldnite copies in their possession or control,
subject to records that must be retained by law or Foldnite's documented
retention policy.

10. SECURITY AND CONFIDENTIALITY

This license does not replace Foldnite security, confidentiality, privacy,
information-governance, or records-retention requirements.

Credentials, API tokens, private keys, protected scientific references,
customer-confidential information, unreleased algorithms, commercial secrets,
and internal deployment secrets must not be disclosed through issues, releases,
